<title>CHINA: Kingboard Chem year net rises 79.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Kingboard Chem year net rises 79.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   30.0   vs 17.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0    vs 4.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    100.40 vs 55.93</p>
<p>    Turnover		     734.38 vs 512.90</p>
<p>    Company name		 Kingboard Chemical Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 6-11</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   August 20</p>
<p>NOTE - Kingboard Chemical Holdings is a manufacturer of laminates.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one 1998 warrant for every five shares held. The warrant carry rights to subscribe for new shares at an initial subscription price of HK$2.40 per share at any time after dealings in the warrants commence -- expected to be August 28, 1997 -- to December 31, 1998.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nine H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs five cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
